Simplest robust fix expressed in the comment:

```dart
// Tree order is NEWEST-FIRST here (the transcript list is reversed);
// identify the tiles by the gate itself instead of by position:
final swappers = tester
    .widgetList<KaomojiSwapper>(find.byType(KaomojiSwapper))
    .toList();
KaomojiFace shown(KaomojiSwapper s) =>
    (tester.widget(find.descendant(
      of: find.byWidget(s),
      matching: find.byWidgetPredicate((w) => w.key is ValueKey<KaomojiFace>),
    )).key! as ValueKey<KaomojiFace>).value;

final live = swappers.singleWhere((s) => s.active);
final finished = swappers.singleWhere((s) => !s.active);
final liveBefore = shown(live);
final finishedBefore = shown(finished);
await tester.pump(kKaomojiSwapPeriod);
expect(shown(finished), same(finishedBefore),
    reason: 'the finished thinking note keeps its frozen face');
expect(shown(live), isNot(same(liveBefore)),
    reason: 'only the LIVE thinking block animates');
```

Caveat: `find.byWidget(s)` — the swapper WIDGET instance in the tree; after the pump, the widget may be a NEW instance (rebuild) — `find.byWidget` matches by widget identity/config equality... KaomojiSwapper doesn't implement == → identity match → after the boundary pump the widget instance might differ → find fails. Safer: capture the Element (`tester.element(find.byType(KaomojiSwapper).at(i))`) and read `element.widget` after the pump, or use `find.byWidgetPredicate` with the active flag... the active flag is on the widget — the state persists so the NEW widget has the same active value: `find.byWidgetPredicate((w) => w is KaomojiSwapper && w.active == false)`. That's robust across rebuilds. I'll present that form.

