    test(1374): wiring test identifies tiles through the gate, not tree order

    Round-3 review: the FaChatScreen transcript renders NEWEST-FIRST, so
    the wiring test's positional [0]/[1] assertions were inverted — [0] is
    the LIVE tile, [1] the finished note. Order was never the contract.

    The stronger contract the review suggested: find each thinking tile's
    KaomojiSwapper by its active flag and assert EXACTLY ONE live swapper
    exists — then assert the single live face moves across the swap
    boundary while the frozen face never does. Order-independent,
    deterministic; test-only, no golden impact.

